---
import ProductLayout from '../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
import data from '../../data/grid/ercot.json';
---
<ProductLayout title="Texas large-load queue" description="A historical ERCOT snapshot of large-load applications through 2033, separated by project stage.">
  <p class="product-note">Historical snapshot as of {data.asOf}, reviewed {data.reviewedAt}. This page does not claim to show the current queue. Applications include uncertain projects and do not equal realized demand.</p>
  <section class="product-section"><h2>{data.total} GW of applications in this snapshot</h2><div class="product-table-wrap"><table class="product-table"><caption>ERCOT April 2026 operational overview, page {data.sourcePage}. Values are rounded by the source.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">GW</th></tr></thead><tbody>{data.stages.map(r=><tr><td>{r.stage}</td><td>{r.value}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
  <section class="product-section"><h2>What the queue can tell a developer</h2><p>The largest application bucket has no studies. That separates early requests from projects closer to grid delivery, but does not assign a completion probability. Watch study progress, required network work and the gap between approval and operation.</p><p>ERCOT’s observed energized measure uses non-simultaneous peaks for fully operational approved loads. It must not be added to, or compared directly with, the simultaneous EIA hourly grid-demand series.</p><p><a href={data.sourceUrl}>Original ERCOT April report (PDF)</a> · <a href="https://www.ercot.com/files/docs/2026/04/16/ERCOT-Monthly-Operational-Overview-March-2026.pdf">Stage definitions in the March report</a> · <a href="https://www.ercot.com/services/rq/large-load-integration/">Large-load integration process</a></p><p class="product-meta">Source: ERCOT. Raw data reproduced with attribution; analysis by Compute Current.</p><a class="product-button" href="/data/ercot.csv" download>Download stage totals CSV</a></section>
</ProductLayout>
